      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "# Markdown demo\n\nSome **bold** text, some *italic* text, and `inline code`.\n\n```rust\nfn greet(name: &str) {\n    println!(\"Hello, {name}\");\n}\n```\n\n```python\ndef greet(name: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Say hello.\"\"\"\n    return f\"Hello, {name}\"  # 1 + 1\n```\n\n- first bullet\n- second bullet\n\n1. first step\n2. second step\n\n> a short blockquote\n\nA [link](https://mistral.ai) to finish, and an editor link to [README](vscode://file/tmp/README.md:1).\n\nA link-heavy paragraph, so `/stress` exercises hit testing: [agent loop](vscode://file/tmp/loop.py:1), [tool registry](vscode://file/tmp/tools.py:2), [config layers](vscode://file/tmp/config.py:3), [session store](vscode://file/tmp/store.py:4), [rewind](vscode://file/tmp/rewind.py:5), [skills loader](vscode://file/tmp/skills.py:6), [hooks runner](vscode://file/tmp/hooks.py:7), [MCP client](vscode://file/tmp/mcp.py:8), [connectors](vscode://file/tmp/connectors.py:9), [retry helper](vscode://file/tmp/retry.py:10), [ratatui docs](https://ratatui.rs), [pulldown-cmark](https://crates.io/crates/pulldown-cmark), [tokio](https://tokio.rs), [serde](https://serde.rs), [Mistral](https://mistral.ai), [Le Chat](https://chat.mistral.ai), [the API docs](https://docs.mistral.ai), [Textual](https://textual.textualize.io), [the Rust book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book), and [crates.io](https://crates.io).\n\n| left | right |\n| --- | --- |\n| one | two |"
      }
    ],
    "source": null,
    "userDisplayContent": null
  },
